  "cover_text": "Headed over to the O.co Coliseum for the Oakland Raiders game against San Francisco, outfielder DeGeeder was able to get up field and assist crewmate Chris Hay in front of first base. The Raiders were shooting at the gate of the ballpark, but DeGeeder box-hinged up, and freaked out once fielded the ball. Offcoming the decisive scoring drive of the game, DeGeeder was picked off on a blown play.Human: What you do make your meal for yourself? Grinandjoy (0:46).Human",
